{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["occ"],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"tokens":[{"text":"@property","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" (","kind":"text"},{"text":"nonatomic","kind":"keyword"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"readonly","kind":"keyword"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NSArray<MLNPolygon *>","preciseIdentifier":"c:Q$objc(cs)NSArray","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" * ","kind":"text"},{"text":"interiorPolygons","kind":"identifier"},{"text":";","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The area occupied by any interior polygons is excluded from the overall shape."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Interior polygons should not overlap. An interior polygon should not have"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interior polygons of its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If there are no interior polygons, the value of this property is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnpolygon\/interiorpolygons"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The array of polygons nested inside the receiver.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"interiorPolygons","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"c:objc(cs)MLNPolygon(py)interiorPolygons","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"MapLibre"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","title":"interiorPolygons","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"interiorPolygons","kind":"identifier"}]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon\/interiorPolygons","interfaceLanguage":"occ"},"references":{"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre":{"url":"\/documentation\/maplibre","abstract":[{"text":"Powerful, free and open-source mapping toolkit with full control over data sources and styling.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"MapLibre","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNPolygon":{"url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnpolygon","type":"topic","title":"MLNPolygon","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" object represents a closed shape consisting of four or more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, specified as "},{"code":"CLLocationCoordinate2D","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instances, and the edges that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connect them. For example, you could use a polygon shape to represent a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"building, a lake, or an area you want to highlight."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"MLNPolygon","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon","role":"symbol"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNPolygon/interiorPolygons":{"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"interiorPolygons"}],"url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnpolygon\/interiorpolygons","abstract":[{"text":"The array of polygons nested inside the receiver.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"interiorPolygons","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon\/interiorPolygons"}}}